SHA256:    fa6741fc4fbd3daebe063acccec0920d72ae5f26c42eb252c85a681397ccc9c0
PRODUCER:  code/S34_a2_normality.R
PRODUCER_SHA256: db3a8099889f9481bc4d36f16cea8a8942327c416b08e32ccb47443267911a7b
INPUTS:
  S1R_ppml.rds: 45c937cd78805d7b13b4c43f4bc4888e93a2ff15e787ad4fb41d77b51f837d89
SEED:      20260731

INPUT PATH NOTE: the producer reads the input from
/scratch/bt307958/ENFORCE_ROOT/data/S1R_ppml.rds, a scratch location that is not
repository-resident and is subject to purge. The script pins the input by SHA256
and halts on mismatch, so the CONTENT is reproducible even though the PATH is
not. A re-run on a different machine must repoint INPUT_PATH at a copy carrying
the SHA above.

SPECIFICATION:
  Tests assumption (A2): log eta_ijt = -sigma^2_ij/2 + u_ijt, u normal.
  Sample: untreated cells only (est_sample & in_model & trade > 0), pairs with
  >= 8 cells. 27,782 pairs used, 10,879 excluded; 570,791 cells used, 43,931
  excluded; 614,722 available.
  Within-pair standardization z = (log eta - mean_i)/sd_i.
  REFERENCE IS A MATCHED NORMAL CONTROL, NOT A THEORETICAL NORMAL: within-pair
  centering and scaling on short windows deforms exactly normal data, so the
  control is drawn pair by pair with identical cell counts and passed through
  identical code. Any deformation the pipeline introduces appears on both sides.

CONTENTS: long format, one row per (panel, year, statistic, grid_point).
  Statistics: rejection_rate (Shapiro-Wilk, 5 pct), skewness, excess_kurtosis,
  quantile (p0.950, p0.990, p0.995, p0.999). Panels: real, control.

HEADLINE VALUES (ledgered SYNC-13):
  rejection_rate real    = 0.327730185011878   [A2_REJECT_REAL]
  rejection_rate control = 0.0502843567777698  [A2_REJECT_CONTROL]
  skewness real          = -0.475527491662458  [A2_SKEW]
  excess kurtosis real   = 0.784025494520271   [A2_EXKURT]
  excess kurtosis ctrl   = -0.269319723301643  [A2_EXKURT_CONTROL]
  quantile ratio p0.99   = 0.9431              [A2_TAIL_RATIO_P99]

DIRECTION NOTE (binding on prose): the departure is left-tailed. The UPPER tail
is THINNER than the control at p0.95, p0.99 and p0.995 (ratios 0.899, 0.943,
0.964), matching only at p0.999 (1.020). Do not describe the log gaps as
heavy-tailed on the right.

GATES:
  G1: |control rejection rate - 0.05| = 0.0003 < 0.02: PASS
  G2: pair/cell accounting reconciles exactly (27782+10879=38661;
      570791+43931=614722): PASS
  G3: identical pair and per-pair cell counts across both panels: PASS
  No gate is placed on the real panel's own values; those are the result.

